# Review handoffs (coordinator rules)

You are the **coordinator and builder**. Full detail: `AGENTS.md`. Dial and caps: `harness/dial.yml`.

## Every round
- Each merge of domain outputs = one round. Commit message MUST contain `[round N]` (N counts up within the PR/iteration).
- Read the dial level for this round (`shallow` scouting / `deep` validating) and say which one you used in the PR body.

## Hand off — do these, do not skip
1. **Every 3rd round** (`audit_every_n_rounds` in `harness/dial.yml`): `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/claude-audit"`.
2. **Deep dial, or before calling anything locked/validated**: `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/claude-audit deep"` AND `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/grok-check deep"`.
3. **Any new/changed physics or source claim** (constant, material value, threshold, mode frequency, validity limit): `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/grok-check"` — Grok is an open channel, use it whenever needed. Run the cheap Tavily filter first (rule 10).
4. **Before merge to main**: latest `/claude-audit` and `/grok-check` on the PR both PASS. If not, fix and re-request.
5. **Reviewers disagree**: `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/claude-audit cross"` and `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/grok-check cross"`.
6. **End of iteration**: `gh pr comment <PR> --body "@claude end-of-iteration review for iteration <K>: file issues for every problem and draft the next change"` or `gh workflow run claude-code-review.yml -f iteration=<K> -f since_ref=iter-<K>-start`.
7. No PR? Use `gh workflow run claude-audit.yml -f depth=<d> -f target_ref=<ref>` / `gh workflow run grok-check.yml -f target_ref=<ref>`, or put `[audit]` in a main commit message.

8. **Optional cheap rote pass** (units, arithmetic, consistency vs `DESIGN_STATE.md`, retired items) any time, e.g. before spending Claude/Grok: `gh pr comment <PR> --body "/deepseek-check"` and/or `"/kimi-check"`. No PR: `gh workflow run deepseek-check.yml -f target_ref=<ref>`. These never replace Claude or Grok and never count toward locked/validated.
9. **Just ask Kimi or DeepSeek a prompt** (no review, nothing posted): `gh workflow run kimi-check.yml -f ping='<prompt>'` / `gh workflow run deepseek-check.yml -f ping='<prompt>'`; reply + token usage + cost are in the run's job summary and the `<reviewer>-ping-<run-id>` artifact.

10. **Web search = Tavily (shared slot). General trigger rule:** whenever a review or check needs current information or external sources (a physics/source claim, a datasheet value, a price, a model or API detail, "is this still true"), use Tavily, not a model's built-in search. Order of spend: Kimi/DeepSeek go through Tavily and filter FIRST (`gh workflow run deepseek-check.yml -f target_ref=<ref> -f search_query='<query>'`, or a `search: <query>` line under `/deepseek-check` / `/kimi-check`; giving a query turns search on), then Claude/Grok spend only on what survives. Grok reviews run one Tavily pre-search by default (query from a `search: <query>` line, else the PR title + changed files); xAI's built-in web search is off. Opt out: `/grok-check nosearch` or `-f web_search=false`. Raw search: `gh workflow run tavily-search.yml -f query='<query>'` or `/tavily-search <query>`. Missing key or Tavily error: skips quietly, never fails a job.

Optional scope: append `domains=thermal,chemical` (or `domains=all`) to `/claude-audit` or `/grok-check`.

## After a verdict
- Read it: `gh pr view <PR> --comments` (or the issue). JSON: `gh run download <run-id>`.
- Fix every `blocker`/`major` finding. Forward Claude's `claims_needing_source_check` to `/grok-check`.
- Report to Danny only when ready (both PASS at deep) or stuck (two FAILs in a row on the same item).

## Never
- Never reintroduce a retired item: oil bath; slotted Cu/Ag shell; ribs/segments; 6.75 kHz (except labelled as history); 0.2 T; 13 GHz atom-count ceiling; cold-regime work; `Backwards_Derived_Spec_from_Ionisation`.
- Never add Perplexity (not in use for now). Qwen is not connected yet: do not wire it without Danny's go-ahead.
- Never let a reviewer edit `.github/workflows/` or merge to main.
